ition\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Acetone forms cyanohydrin, which is homologated/reduced and then desulfurized to isobutyraldehyde via Cu(I)/Cu(II) photoredox catalysis under UV.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Directly shown by Patel et al. 2015 (Nature Chemistry) and Liu et al. 2023; need for H2S/HS- and staged reagent addition is a critique.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_005\",\n      \"name\": \"Fischer\u2013Tropsch-type synthesis of aldehydes\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_001\", \"mol_002\", \"mol_003\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_009\", \"mol_013\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Hydrothermal\",\n      \"agents\": [\"Fe\u2013Ni metal (native/mineral)\"],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"470-600K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"high\",\n        \"catalyst\": \"Fe\u2013Ni native alloy\",\n        \"aqueous\": false,\n        \"other\": \"Black smoker or vent interior\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"CO + H2 + NH3 yields C4/C5 aldehydes (branched and linear) via surface catalyzed reduction.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Demonstrated for amino acid precursors in Yoshino et al. 1971, though valine is a minor product and selectivity low; still possible in high-temperature Fe\u2013Ni-rich zones.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rxn_006\",\n      \"name\": \"Reductive amination of \u03b1-ketoisovalerate to valine\",\n      \"inputs\": [\"mol_010\", \"mol_003\", \"H2\"],\n      \"outputs\": [\"mol_011\"],\n      \"environment\": \"Hydrothermal\",\n      \"agents\": [\"Ni/SiO2-Al2O3\", \"Aletai iron meteorite\", \"Pd/C\"],\n      \"conditions\": {\n        \"temperature\": \"295-330K\",\n        \"pressure\": \"elevated (~5 bar H2)\",\n        \"catalyst\": \"Nickel, iron-nickel meteorite, or Pd\",\n        \"aqueous\": true,\n        \"other\": \"NH4HCO3 buffer, pH 8\"\n      },\n      \"mechanism\": \"Imine formation from ketoacid and ammonia, followed by metal-catalyzed reduction to form valine.\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Directly demonstrate